Subject: bio: exclude AF_UNIX path under __wasi__

WASI's sockaddr_un is intentionally stripped (only sun_family, no
sun_path) because WASI has no Unix-domain sockets. AWS-LC's guard in
crypto/bio/internal.h triggers on `defined(AF_UNIX)` alone — which
wasi-libc still defines as a constant (= 3) for ABI shape, even
though the supporting struct is gutted. The guard then enables code
in bio_addr.c that touches `.sun_path`, breaking compilation.

Add __wasi__ to the exclusion list alongside Windows and Android,
both of which AWS-LC already documents as Unix-sockets-incapable.

--- a/crypto/bio/internal.h
+++ b/crypto/bio/internal.h
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ int BIO_socket_nbio(int sock, int on);
 // and the last socket error indicates that it's non-fatal.
 int bio_socket_should_retry(int return_value);

-#if defined(AF_UNIX) && !defined(OPENSSL_WINDOWS) && !defined(OPENSSL_ANDROID)
+#if defined(AF_UNIX) && !defined(OPENSSL_WINDOWS) && !defined(OPENSSL_ANDROID) && !defined(__wasi__)
   // Winsock2 APIs don't support AF_UNIX.
   // > The values currently supported are AF_INET or AF_INET6, which are the
   // > Internet address family formats for IPv4 and IPv6.
